      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-26T18:36:44Z",
      "note": "VSCTokenManager was deployed directly at block 10703671:102. Its runtime hashes to 0x278126dd080cc987ad5f11032088cb529ecd1dedde6b24a30d1fd11de2b20645 at deployment and before the exploit. Transaction 0xda2a8568a5a210fdfb51880f4e8c91165ea122ada9977a4b11598d56782d49a5 at block 20519307:107 called VOWToken.setUSDRate(1,100), changing storage slots 0xb and 0xc from 5 and 1 to 1 and 100. The declared getVOWVSCRate() call returns [5,1] at block 20519306 and [1,100] at block 20519307. The manager emitted no burn-and-mint event before the anchor in the three-block window. At block 20519309:1, the exploit trace calls VSCTokenManager through VOW's ERC-777 receive hook, burns 1,486,625.296150499360431664 VOW, and mints 148,662,529.615049936043166400 vUSD. After swaps and flash repayment, receipt transfers and native-value traces show the exact three declared proceeds reaching the attacker EOA. Chainlink feed 0x5f4ec3df9cbd43714fe2740f5e3616155c5b8419 returned 263651460000 with 8 decimals and updatedAt 1723546535 at the anchor block."
    }
